# Known violations of the CSS architecture contract (web/css/README.md).
#
# Format: <check> <item>   # optional note
#
# This file is the outstanding debt of the CSS restructure. Entries may be
# removed, never added: a new violation is a build failure, and an entry that
# stops matching anything is also a failure, so the file cannot rot.
#
# The ownership block arrived in one go when the sheets were split and every
# `"owns": ["*"]` became a real list of roots. Until then the check could not
# see anything — one file owning everything cannot misfile a rule. Nothing got
# worse that day; the debt simply became countable. It only shrinks from here.
#
# Audit what is still owed:  node scripts/lint-css-arch --emit-allowlist

# --- token-parity ---------------------------------------------------------
# Theme-independent tokens that share the dark theme's :root block only because
# dark was written first. They move to tokens/scale.css.
token-parity --modal-scrim
token-parity --overlay-dark-70
token-parity --overlay-dark-50
token-parity --overlay-dark-25
token-parity --overlay-dark-15
token-parity --overlay-dark-10


# --- ownership ------------------------------------------------------------
# A selector filed where manifest.json says another sheet owns its root.
# Each line is one root in one sheet, and each names a rule that has not been
# moved to its group yet.

# A group whose rules the old files had in several places, so the split had to
# cut it across numbered sheets. Defragmenting merges each set into one.
ownership components/approvals-2.css:textarea
ownership components/composer.css:conversation-area
ownership components/messages-1.css:conversation-area
ownership components/messages-2.css:thread-message
ownership components/messages-3.css:tool-group-message
ownership components/model-picker.css:composer-box
ownership components/properties-panel.css:settings-panel
ownership components/settings-1.css:settings-panel
ownership components/settings-3.css:commands-menu
ownership components/settings-3.css:find-bar
ownership components/settings-3.css:settings-panel
ownership components/strategy-bar.css:composer-box

# Cross-cutting policy that names every component it applies to — the text
# selection rules and the menu system in app-shell, and the app-wide @media
# stack in responsive. These move to the components they modify, which is what
# empties layout/responsive.css entirely.
ownership layout/app-shell.css:app-header
ownership layout/app-shell.css:conversation-tab
ownership layout/app-shell.css:window-mode
ownership patterns/markdown.css:window-mode

# Roots several unrelated components style, which is the definition of a
# pattern: they want a patterns/ file of their own rather than an owner.
ownership base/reset.css:button
ownership base/reset.css:input
ownership base/reset.css:textarea
