# --- layer-inversion -------------------------------------------------------
# A rule filed below a rule it overrides: the lower-layer rule wins today by
# being more specific, and would lose the moment the sheets are wrapped in
# their layers. One entry per file pair, `<lower> > <higher> <count>`, because
# the fix is per file pair and the findings run to thousands.
#
# The count is a ratchet: exceeding it fails, and so does beating it — the
# number comes down with the work. To see what is behind one:
#
#   node scripts/lint-css-arch --inversions <lower> <higher>
#
# What is left here is not a list of mistakes to fix one at a time. It is two
# things: component base styles sitting in utilities/ where a component cannot
# reach them, and cross-cutting policy filed in layout/ instead of in the
# components it modifies. Re-classifying and re-filing those empties the block.
# (Deleting the dead CSS already took it from 33,908 to 14,828.)
